<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmond van Eetvelde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1852–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmond van Eetvelde was a Belgian official who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii">Leopold II</a> as administrator-general of foreign affairs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> from 1885 and as its secretary of state from 1894. Working from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, he was one of the chief architects of the state's administration and of its diplomacy with the European powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmond-van-eetvelde.jpg" alt="Edmond van Eetvelde" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edmond_van_Eetvelde2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
